# What graphify should NOT index.
#
# This is deliberately different from .gitignore. Both directories below are
# legitimately tracked in git and must stay tracked. They just have no business
# in a knowledge graph whose purpose is navigating OUR work.
#
# Measured on the 2026-09-03 rebuild, before this file existed:
#   third_party  540 nodes  61.0%
#   references   221 nodes  25.0%
#   report        29 nodes   3.3%   <- the entire literature survey
# 86% of the graph was material we either never edit or did not write, and the
# god-node list came back as Uint128 / Share128 / PowerIteration(), which are
# Nudge's Go internals rather than anything in this project.

# Vendored Nudge reference implementation. ~10.7K lines of Go, CGo and assembly.
# CLAUDE.md makes it a black box we never edit, so indexing its call graph
# actively buries our own material.
third_party/

# The 40 acquired paper PDFs. They are the survey's evidence base, not its
# structure. What we concluded from them lives in report/notes/evidence.md and
# report/sections/, which ARE indexed.
references/

# Build artefacts and caches.
graphify-out/
**/*.aux
**/*.log
**/*.fls
**/*.fdb_latexmk
**/*.synctex.gz
**/*.nav
**/*.snm
**/*.toc
**/*.out
**/*.bbl
**/*.blg

# Browser "save page as" support directories. `docs/artifacts/` holds one saved
# rendering of the pipeline diagram; the sibling `_files/` folder beside it is
# minified vendor JS, a Google Fonts css2 response, and two `saved_resource`
# stubs that are fragments of the SAME page. Indexing them gave three duplicate
# nodes ("OblivRec Pipeline", "Nudge (USENIX Sec '26)", "PRAC") that shadowed
# the real diagram, and `saved_resource(1).html` dispatched to the LLM on every
# extraction only to return nothing. The page itself stays indexed.
docs/artifacts/**/*_files/
